# Ready-made requests for VS Code "REST Client" or JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Start the service first, e.g.: docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 -e PUBLISHER=log ubl-order-transformer

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Valid order (business message posted directly) -> 200 + transformed order
POST {{baseUrl}}/pubsub/push
Content-Type: application/json

< ./samples/messages/valid-order.json

### Valid order wrapped in a Pub/Sub push envelope (what Cloud Run receives) -> 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/pubsub/push
Content-Type: application/json

< ./samples/messages/pubsub-push-envelope.json

### Single order line, other unit of measure -> 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/pubsub/push
Content-Type: application/json

< ./samples/messages/valid-order-single-line.json

### Invalid Base64 -> 400 InvalidBase64
POST {{baseUrl}}/pubsub/push
Content-Type: application/json

< ./samples/messages/invalid-base64.json

### Invalid XML -> 400 InvalidXml
POST {{baseUrl}}/pubsub/push
Content-Type: application/json

< ./samples/messages/invalid-xml.json

### Missing Order/ID -> 400 ValidationError "Order ID is required."
POST {{baseUrl}}/pubsub/push
Content-Type: application/json

< ./samples/messages/missing-order-id.json

### Missing document -> 400 ValidationError "document is required."
POST {{baseUrl}}/pubsub/push
Content-Type: application/json

< ./samples/messages/missing-document.json
